<title>POLAND: Polish wheat, rye prices ease, barley up last week.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat, rye prices ease, barley up last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that wheat and rye prices slipped while barley prices inched up during last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p> Product   week to Feb 22    previous week	 yr/yr growth</p>
<p> Wheat	56.53 zl/q	  56.79 zl/q		7.5 pct</p>
<p> Rye	  42.04 zl/q	  42.20 zl/q	     27.3 pct</p>
<p> Barley     49.65 zl/q	  49.37 zl/q		8.7 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
